    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-2" id="fn-2" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Property under Operating Leases, $ 232,006,789</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-3" id="fn-3" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Obligations under Operating Leases - Non-Current, $200,642,095</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-4" id="fn-4" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Obligations under Operating Leases - Current, $27,585,238</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-5" id="fn-5" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Property under Operating Leases, $ 232,006,789</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-6" id="fn-6" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">$23K was a prior period nuclear refueling outage adjustment.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-7" id="fn-7" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Property under Capital Leases of $244,817,753 is not included in this total.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-8" id="fn-8" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">(1) Customer 360 Deferred Costs amortized over 15 years beginning May 2017 and ending in 2032.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-9" id="fn-9" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">(2) The Charging Forward program was initially approved in Case U-20162.&#160; Costs have been recorded in annual layers beginning in 2019 and included in subsequent rate cases for approval, to be amortized over 5 year periods.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-10" id="fn-10" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">(3) Advanced Distribution Management System includes various upgrades for which costs have been separately deferred and are being amortized over respective 15 year periods through 2038.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-11" id="fn-11" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">(4) Advanced Customer Pricing Pilot amortized over 5 years beginning December 2022 and ending in 2027.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-12" id="fn-12" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">(5) Demand Response annual layers are being amortized over respective 3 year periods.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-13" id="fn-13" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">(6) Low Income Payment Stability is being amortized over 2 years beginning March 2026.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-14" id="fn-14" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">(7) Time of Day Rate Implementation amortized over 5 years beginning December 2023 and ending in 2028.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-15" id="fn-15" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Note: Above docket numbers refer to original authorization of regulatory asset.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-16" id="fn-16" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">(8) Recoverable Income Taxes are being amortized over 28 years ending in 2028.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-17" id="fn-17" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">(9) Monroe Non Securitized Regulatory Asset being amortized over 15 years beginning February 2025.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-18" id="fn-18" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">(10) $10.526M of Residential Income Assistance is being amortized over 5 years beginning March 2026.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-19" id="fn-19" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">(1) Beginning May 2019, amounts are being amortized over various periods for plant and non-plant accumulated deferred income tax balances.&#160; Amortization is estimated to continue through 2062.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-20" id="fn-20" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">(2) Incentives Tracker annual layers are being amortized over respective 5 year periods ending in February 2031.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-21" id="fn-21" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">(3) Beginning December 2023, the amount is being amortized over 7 years.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-22" id="fn-22" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">(4) Per ASU 2017-07 relating to financing costs not being eligible for capitalization.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-23" id="fn-23" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">(5) Beginning March 2026, $1.045M is being amortized over 5 years.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-24" id="fn-24" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Note: Above docket numbers refer to original authorization of regulatory liability.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-25" id="fn-25" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Total includes the following amounts: $8,090,424 Contribution in Aid of Construction, $499,087 Reconnection Fees, $274,075 New Service Charge,&#160; $157,334 AMI Opt Out Fees,$147,441 Unauthorized Use, and $143,023 of items that do not individually meet the $250,000 threshold.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-26" id="fn-26" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Total includes the following amounts: $51,814,407 Renewable ITC Revenue Timing Adjustment (Interim only), $2,100,196 Steam Sales, $367,693 Sales &amp; Use Tax Collection Fees, $162,000 Service Charge for Returned Checks, $134,223 Insight Bridge Charges, $129,675 Securitization Servicing Fees, $12,350 Unauthorized Use Charge, and $283,562 of items that do not individually meet the $250,000 threshold.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-27" id="fn-27" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Consists of $30,109,488 Electric Choice Revenue, and $239,841 Wholesale Delivery Services Revenue.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-28" id="fn-28" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">This revenue represents our sales to MISO, our area's independent grid operator.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-29" id="fn-29" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The activity in rows 2-9 relates to renewable energy purchase power agreements.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-30" id="fn-30" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Blue Water Renewables, Inc is a wholly owned, indirect subsidiary of DTE Energy Company.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-31" id="fn-31" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Big Turtle is a wholly owned, indirect subsidiary of DTE Energy Company.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-32" id="fn-32" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The activity in rows 10-13 relates to test energy transferred to offset capital costs.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-33" id="fn-33" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">See Footnote on Page 300, Line 22, Column b.</link:footnote>
